// Data-driven debug map warp list for the client's "Maps" window.
//
// Loaded through the normal game file loader (`data\client\debug_maps.ron`) so
// a server can override it inside its own archive without rebuilding the
// client; the same file is embedded with `include_str!` as the compiled
// fallback (`korangar/src/client_config/debug_maps.rs`).
//
// This is a **debug-only convenience** list (the Maps window is a developer
// window, see `korangar/tests/ui_consistency.rs::DEBUG_ONLY_FILES`), not
// shipped user-facing content: it exists so a tester can jump to the main towns
// quickly. The warp is sent as the server-side `@warp`/`WarpToMap` request.
//
// Facts (hand-curated from the previous Rust array
// `korangar/src/interface/windows/maps.rs::MAP_WARPS`, 23 map/coordinate pairs;
// no game data was extracted for this file). The coordinates are the classic
// town-centre spawn cells.
//
// Validation is strict (`deny_unknown_fields`, non-empty list, unique map
// names, positive coordinates); a malformed archive override is logged and the
// compiled fallback is used.
// `korangar --check-debug-maps [PATH]` validates this file without starting a
// window.
(
    provenance: "hand-curated debug warp list from the former maps.rs MAP_WARPS array (23 maps); debug-only convenience, no game data extraction",
    version: 1,
    maps: [
